id: pm-brand-semantic-asset-change-reports
title: Explain semantic changes between generated SVG assets
description: "Read-only, bounded SVG review evidence for visible text, token roles, geometry and accessible labels."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: assets,cli,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-29T00:47:34.875Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T06:47:10.910Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Attribute reordering yields zero semantic changes; a changed status color and truncated label yield two localized findings; no raster generation or network is needed; typed SDK and CLI expose bounded JSON and TOON with typed refusals and remedies; validate public tracker assets on a read-only non-git copy.
comments[26]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T00:47:58.698Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against installed pm SDK declarations, pm-brand generators and diagnostics, pm-vcs vcs diff, pm-gantt-chart rendering, and pm-graph snapshot impact. No SVG semantic comparator exists. pm-vcs owns versioned bytes and generic diffs; this feature supplies bounded static asset review evidence. Reuse the existing lazy public SDK loader, attachOutputTokenAccounting and TOON encoder. Pure read-only input/output: no tracker writes, journal, imports, sync, status interpretation or shared mutable state in the product path; transaction isolation is not claimed. Unsupported SVG constructs will refuse with a remedy rather than silently omit rendering effects."
  "2026-10-29T01:01:59.105Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed compareSemanticAssets/renderSemanticAssetReport plus semantic-diff CLI, strict bounded static SVG grammar, grouped visible outline metadata and geometry digests, localized text/token/geometry/accessibility evidence, JSON/TOON output via SDK accounting, typed refusals and remedies. Focused 15/15 tests, typecheck, lint and docstrings passed. New modules measured 100/100/100/100 coverage. The 500-sequence model completed 6000 transitions, 997 older-input replays and 500 complete native SDK read-backs with relationships, fields and ambient focus preserved. Behavioral reverts caught 4/4 independent faults; restored implementation passed the unchanged regressions. Public read-only non-git tracker: 16 items, 48 generated source assets, 48 comparisons (16 identity/0 changes, 16 serialization/0 changes, 16 edits/32 findings), 96 reports, max 94 SDK estimated tokens/375 bytes, zero budget refusals; SDK state and byte hashes unchanged. See docs/semantic-assets-validation.md. Runtime is read-only and creates no import/export/sync journal, idempotency key, claim, lease or shared product state. No transaction-isolation or atomic snapshot claim; each supplied SVG string is caller-owned input. Full npm/Bun release gates are delegated to exact-head CI per the host resource constraint."
  "2026-10-29T01:04:57.911Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brand/pull/27 . Linked tests ran through pinned pm: 1/1 command passed, 15/15 tests, zero skips/failures. Test-result tracking is disabled by the existing project policy, so this comment records the successful run without changing that policy. Isolated-home strict tracker health passed; the ordinary home exposed an ambient pm-github host-version mismatch (pinned host versus newer global extension), not tracker corruption. Four behavioral reverts passed again after final implementation changes; two image regressions passed. All 52 generated banners match main byte-for-byte after removing only the new data-text metadata. Extended numeric fuzz checks geometry coordinate, size and opacity domains as well as input budgets and emitted counts. Claim is released for orchestrator review; item remains in progress. Final exact-head npm/Bun release-gate results and run links are reported on the PR checks/description: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brand/pull/27/checks . No merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-29T01:10:07.899Z",codex-agent,"Final review added regressions preserving visible non-breaking/Unicode spaces and refusing malformed numeric separators. Updated focused suite: 16/16 passed (including the unchanged 500-sequence model). Current CLI 2026.10.28 help was also inspected: semantic retrieval is item search; no SVG/asset comparison command overlaps this feature. Typecheck and lint passed after these corrections. Revert proof now includes the Unicode-space fault: 5/5 caught, with 3/3 restored acceptance regressions passing. Public read-only validation metrics remain documented separately; final exact-head CI links and counts will be placed on PR 27 after all tracker writes are committed."
  "2026-10-29T02:14:28.884Z",codex-agent,"Resumed review round 1. Worktree was clean; origin/main is already an ancestor (3 branch commits, zero behind), so no merge is required. Two confirmed rule classes: semantic identity must retain topology/ancestor context, and grammar-specific lexical domains must be validated before numeric canonicalization. Audit will cover every comparison/parser entry, JSON/TOON and CLI, grouped outlines, packed npm/Bun consumers and non-git execution. Existing regressions remain intact; new adversarial properties and disposable behavioral reverts will prove these classes."
  "2026-10-29T02:30:59.143Z",codex-agent,"Class audit completed across all src, scripts and tests: only semantic-assets/static-svg own semantic topology and SVG number grammar; root exports, subpath exports and CLI call those same functions. Fixed retained-node parent evidence (including metadata and grouped outlines) and common-child ordering even with simultaneous membership changes; kept one-finding insertion behavior and all existing tests unchanged. Lexical validation now precedes canonicalization for both arc flags and unsigned radii, numeric-list separators, XML syntax/id whitespace, plus shared contrast/CSS whitespace. Other conversions already follow validated integer/hex/entity schemas; text wrapping intentionally segments natural language rather than parsing geometry. One validated request context is retained for JSON/TOON SVG refusals. New tests first failed on the old implementation (zero-findings reparenting and accepted invalid flags), then the focused 21/21 passed. Independent topology model: 500 sequences, 4000 transitions, 802 old-input replays; original model remains 500/6000/997 with complete native SDK read-back. No additional non-blocking findings were present in the provided review or PR review threads. Packed acceptance now carries six representative review cases through all six installation modes and both encodings; package/Git SDK consumers and direct Bun share the same fixture producer."
  "2026-10-29T02:42:16.015Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof on the corrected implementation: node scripts/semantic-assets-revert-proof.ts caught 15/15 isolated behavioral reverts and the restored implementation passed 6/6 selected regressions. Specifically, deleting parent comparison fails the independent topology model; restoring the equal-membership-only ordering rule fails the shared adversarial corpus; coercing either arc flag before validation fails the 500-probe contextual flag property. Additional independent reverts cover unsigned radii, numeric/XML/CSS separators, invalid id trimming and lost refusal format. The first new tests failed on the original implementation before the fix. All three changed runtime modules measure 100/100/100/100 at unchanged thresholds. Pinned pm linked runner passed 2/2 commands: 16/16 original tests plus 10/10 review/contrast tests, zero skips/failures. Typecheck, lint and docstrings passed. Read-only public validation retains 16 items/48 original comparisons/32 findings/96 reports (max 94 tokens/375 bytes) and adds 16 reparent findings plus 16 arc refusals in 64 reports (max 91 tokens/361 bytes); complete SDK state and tracker byte hash are unchanged. See updated docs/semantic-assets-validation.md. Full npm/Bun gates run in CI with the existing two-worker coverage runner to honor the host CPU constraint. Final-head results will be recorded in PR 27 after tracker writes are complete."
  "2026-10-29T03:21:31.852Z",codex-agent,"Resumed review round 2. Worktree was clean; origin/main is already an ancestor (4 branch commits, zero behind), so no merge is required. General rule: a canonical projection must preserve semantically significant order even for children that do not paint pixels. Audit confirms title/desc are the supported metadata children currently filtered out of the only child-order stream; this also affects grouped outline metadata and mixed membership/order changes. The fix will retain complete child order and derive paint, title and description order separately through the shared SDK/CLI comparison path. ARIA reference-list order is already retained as field text and will receive controls. The supplied review has one blocker and no additional non-blocking findings; PR review threads are empty. Existing fixes and tests remain intact."
  "2026-10-29T03:28:25.697Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 class audit and regression: identified-title swap initially failed with zero findings before the fix. Canonical nodes now retain all direct child source order; the comparator derives paint, title and description streams separately, and grouped outlines discard only glyph paths while preserving metadata order. Both title and desc order, root/group/outlined containers, mixed insertion/removal plus reordering, and ordered aria-labelledby/aria-describedby references are covered. Existing state/geometry/lexical tests remain unchanged. The first corrected focused run passed 18/18 tests. A new independent metadata model completed 500 sequences, 4000 transitions, 822 older-input replays and 756 order findings; all six container/type domains are checked. Shared SDK/CLI fixture cases now include metadata order and unchanged cross-type controls; packed/Git SDK consumers, direct Bun and all six CLI installation modes reuse them. No new request schema, SDK acquisition path or mutable tracker state was introduced."
  "2026-10-29T03:36:07.988Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 verification complete. node scripts/semantic-assets-revert-proof.ts caught 20/20 independent behavioral reverts and the restored implementation passed 7/7 selected regressions. New class-specific proofs independently discard non-painting child order (the 500-sequence metadata model fails), sort away title order, sort away description order, clear metadata during outline grouping, and misclassify metadata as paint; each is caught. Both changed runtime modules measure 100/100/100/100 at unchanged thresholds. Pinned pm linked runner passed 2/2 commands: 16/16 existing acceptance tests and 12/12 review/contrast tests, zero skips/failures. Typecheck, lint and docstrings passed. Shared corpus now has 94 cases; nine representative semantic cases run across six packed CLI modes and both encodings (156 command-format scenarios per gate including the existing diagnostics). Public read-only copy retains all baseline and round-1 results and adds 16 title-order plus 16 description-order comparisons yielding 32 localized accessibility findings and 64 reports (max 58 SDK estimated tokens/230 bytes). Complete SDK read-back and the public tracker byte hash remain unchanged; runtime raster/network calls remain zero. All tracker writes finish before final-head CI; exact npm/Bun run links and counts will be added to PR 27. Claim released for orchestrator re-review; item remains in progress."
  "2026-10-29T04:02:27.445Z",codex-agent,"Review round 3: branch is current with origin/main; no merge needed. Reclaimed the existing item. General rule: validate XML lexical context before entity expansion; document prolog/epilog permit literal XML whitespace and comments, never references. Package audit found the single shared static SVG parser is used by root/subpath SDK, JSON/TOON, non-git CLI, packed npm/Bun and Git consumers; no parallel decoder exists. Audit will cover both input sides, both document boundaries, comments/declarations, legal inner references, independent parser validation and seeded adversarial cases. No additional non-blocking review threads were supplied or found. Prior acceptance and replay models remain intact."
  "2026-10-29T04:07:52.816Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 implementation: raw prolog/epilog text must be literal XML whitespace before any entity expansion; the single shared parser now rejects all outside-root references. Legal inner text/attributes, comments, declarations, BOM and CRLF controls are preserved. Added 80 malformed cases across decimal/hex/zero-padded whitespace references, both edges, comments and both inputs plus six positive controls; shared corpus now 180 cases and packed representatives 13 (204 command-format scenarios per full gate). An independent offline Resvg parser checks the same XML domain without raster generation/system fonts. New model: 500 sequences, 4000 transitions, 817 older-input replays, 1440 typed refusals, complete JSON/TOON agreement. Original tests were retained. No mutable tracker, acquisition, sync or concurrency path changed."
  "2026-10-29T04:07:53.919Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: new document-boundary test failed on the prior implementation with a successful report instead of unsupported_svg. The disposable revert script then restored the original decode-before-context behavior inside parseStaticSvg, rebuilt dist, and the adversarial regression failed. All 21 independent behavioral reverts were caught; fixed code restored in finally and all 8 selected regressions passed afterward. Focused coverage command: node node_modules/c8/bin/c8.js --include=dist/semantic-assets.js --include=dist/static-svg.js --reporter=text --reporter=json node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/semantic-assets.test.ts test/semantic-review.test.ts: 20/20 passed; both modules 100/100/100/100. Typecheck, lint, docstrings and build:check passed. build:check compares the staged compiled output against a clean build; initial unstaged-output check correctly reported pending compiled changes."
  "2026-10-29T04:07:54.835Z",codex-agent,"Repeated read-only public main tracker validation: 16 items, 48 generated source assets, 48 original comparisons, 32 localized color/text findings, 96 reports, zero noise findings/budget refusals, max 94 estimated tokens/375 bytes. Existing parent/arc and metadata probes stayed unchanged. New prefix/suffix probes: 32 comparisons, 32 typed refusals, 64 reports, max 91 estimated tokens/361 bytes. Complete SDK read-back and tracker-byte SHA256 stayed unchanged; runtime raster/network calls 0. Evidence and public source provenance are in docs/semantic-assets-validation.md. Full npm/Bun gates run in exact-head CI with the existing two-worker coverage runner; final run URL, pass counts and captured artifact digest will be recorded on PR 27 after the final push."
  "2026-10-29T04:08:22.714Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm linked runner: 2/2 commands passed, zero skipped or failed. Exact commands: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/semantic-assets.test.ts test/package-banners.test.ts (16/16); node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/semantic-review.test.ts test/contrast.test.ts (14/14). Tracking policy disables automatic test-result persistence, so these receipts are recorded explicitly here. Source/compiled modules, shared consumer fixtures, adversarial/replay tests, revert script and reproduction docs are linked. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress. No known pm SDK defect or unresolved review finding remains; bounded static SVG grammar is documented. Latest exact-head CI evidence will be on PR 27."
  "2026-10-29T04:26:35.418Z",codex-agent,"Review round 4: current with origin/main, clean at resume; reclaimed existing item. General rule: XML lexical validity and decoding belong to a maintained standards parser, with attribute/text context kept distinct. Whole-package audit found only static-svg owns XML decoding; all SDK/CLI, JSON/TOON, packed npm/Bun, Git and non-git consumers share it. Replace the hand-written XML tokenizer/decoder with @xmldom/xmldom using a strict error handler; no entity resolvers or I/O, explicit byte/node/depth/attribute limits, namespace-aware canonical projection. Add escaping/CDATA/PI/namespace/BOM/CRLF conformance pairs, equivalent serialization model, malformed controls and behavioral replacement proof. Previous topology, metadata, arc and document-boundary regressions remain required. No additional non-blocking review threads were supplied or found."
  "2026-10-29T04:31:39.492Z",codex-agent,"Parser selection evidence: xmldom strict-error probes accepted forbidden literal character-data terminators and illegal control-character references; saxes upstream is archived. Chose @rgrove/parse-xml 5.0.0 instead: actively maintained, pure JS, zero dependencies, XML 1.0 conformance corpus, no DTD loading or custom entity expansion. Installed with lifecycle scripts disabled and no inherited package-manager credentials. Removed the hand-written XML decoder/tokenizer; the dependency now owns contextual escaping, CDATA/comments/PI, BOM, declarations and line endings. Well-formed constructs outside our documented semantic domain retain refusal under new unsupported_semantics; unsupported_svg is reserved for XML parser rejection or resource limits. Existing refusal tests retain every input, side, remedy and format assertion and now assert the stronger exact distinction."
  "2026-10-29T04:44:16.708Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 implementation and class audit complete: no hand-written XML decoder/tokenizer remains. Maintained parser handles attribute/text escaping (literal attribute CDATA terminator included), numeric/hex references, CDATA, comments, PI, BOM and CRLF. SVG projection resolves default/prefixed/inherited namespace bindings and rejects reserved or foreign bindings before interpretation. Explicit limits: 1 MiB input, 4096 elements, depth 32, 32 attributes and 32768 geometry lexemes. DTD/custom-entity resolution and all network/file access are absent. Shared corpus: 234 cases, including 54 XML conformance pairs; 17 representatives propagate through non-git CLI, packed npm/Bun, npx/bunx and Git SDK consumers (252 command-format scenarios per full gate). New equivalent-serialization model: 500 sequences, 4000 transitions, 808 older-input replays, zero findings, JSON/TOON round trips and exact raw accessible-label preservation. Strengthened decoded-value and changed-CDATA assertions after a lossy-parser mutation exposed that equality alone could hide dropped text. Existing acceptance/refusal/replay inputs retained; exact typed refusal distinction updated rather than weakened."
  "2026-10-29T04:45:55.780Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 revert proof passed: node scripts/semantic-assets-revert-proof.ts caught 26/26 behavioral reverts/replacements in disposable copies and restored code passed 10/10 selected regressions. The full previous parser from commit 7e7690f was rebuilt with only a refusal-shape adapter, and the new conformance/value-preservation tests failed; fixed parser restored in finally. Adapted prior mutation anchors to the maintained parser/projection without removing the original regression cases. Focused C8 run selected 15 deterministic boundary/conformance tests: 15/15 passed, both semantic modules 100/100/100/100. Typecheck, lint, docstrings and build:check passed (30 compiled files match a clean build). No-I/O claims refer specifically to XML external-resource resolution; the CLI still reads its explicitly requested input file and the output layer uses the supported lazy SDK loader."
  "2026-10-29T04:45:58.190Z",codex-agent,"Round 4 public validation repeated on the read-only, non-git main tracker copy: 16 native items, 48 generated assets, 48 original comparisons, 32 color/text findings, 96 reports, zero noise findings and budget refusals; max 94 tokens/375 bytes. Existing parent/arc probes: 64 reports, max 63 tokens/251 bytes; metadata: 64 reports, max 58/230; boundary: 32 typed refusals, 64 reports, max 53/211. New XML-equivalent title-derived probes: 16 comparisons, zero findings, 32 reports, max 21 tokens/83 bytes. Complete SDK read-back and tracker-byte hash unchanged, runtime raster/network calls 0. Full npm/Bun release gates remain delegated to exact-head CI with two-worker coverage; the PR will hold the final run URL, counts and artifact digest after the final push."
  "2026-10-29T04:47:00.639Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm linked tests: 2/2 commands passed with zero skipped, failed or timed out. node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/semantic-assets.test.ts test/package-banners.test.ts: 16/16. node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/semantic-review.test.ts test/contrast.test.ts: 18/18, including all seeded models and non-git CLI. Automatic result tracking is disabled by existing project policy; results recorded explicitly here. All changed source, compiled modules, dependency lock, shared consumer fixtures, docs and tests are linked. No known pm SDK defect found. No further review findings supplied. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item stays in progress. Final exact-head CI evidence will be recorded on PR 27."
  "2026-10-29T06:30:11.405Z",codex-agent,"Review round 5: clean resume at 59ab17b, current with origin/main (no merge needed), existing item reclaimed. General rule: element identity includes its resolved namespace URI; legacy bare-SVG compatibility must not reactivate after entering the SVG namespace. Package audit found one canonical projection, shared by SDK root/subpath, CLI, JSON/TOON, packed npm/Bun, Git and non-git consumers. Audit covers empty resets, missing default namespaces beneath prefixed SVG elements, namespace-qualified controls, every supported element and annotated outlines. Maintain the prior bare/root-empty fixtures; carry independent namespace inheritance/replay tests and revert proofs through all consumers. No additional non-blocking findings supplied or present in review threads."
  "2026-10-29T06:43:15.952Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 class fix: namespace resolution retains an ancestry-scoped legacy flag; actual SVG namespace entry disables bare-name promotion for descendants. Empty resets and missing defaults under qualified SVG parents refuse unsupported_semantics, including grouped outline paths. Qualified SVG names under empty defaults, explicit default restoration, legacy root-empty fixtures and independent sibling scopes remain valid. Shared corpus now 336 cases (102 namespace cases); 22 packed representatives imply 312 command-format scenarios per full gate. Independent Resvg geometry model: 500 sequences, 4000 transitions, 796 older-input replays, 2362 accepted and 1638 refusals, with no rasters/fonts. Focused C8: 16/16 passed, both semantic modules 100/100/100/100. Typecheck, lint, docstrings and build:check passed; 30 compiled files match a clean build."
  "2026-10-29T06:43:26.252Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 revert proof: namespace identity regression failed on the previous head with a successful zero-change report. node scripts/semantic-assets-revert-proof.ts caught 29/29 behavioral reverts/replacements; fixed code restored in finally, 11/11 selected regressions passed afterward. New mutations reinstate unconditional absent-URI promotion, reset legacy mode per child, or infer a default namespace from a qualified parent. Existing regressions and all earlier mutation probes retained. Pinned linked test 1 passed 16/16; linked test 2 reached the local runner default 120-second timeout under shared-host load, with no assertion failure recorded. Re-running only test 2 with a 300-second harness budget; assertion, numeric-performance and coverage thresholds are unchanged. Recording this timeout rather than hiding it."
  "2026-10-29T06:46:13.925Z",codex-agent,"Round 5 read-only public main tracker validation passed: 16 items, 48 original source assets, 48 original comparisons, zero serialization-noise findings, 32 localized color/text findings and 96 reports, max 94 estimated tokens/375 bytes. New namespace probes: 48 comparisons, 32 unsupported_semantics refusals for empty resets/missing defaults, 16 unchanged qualified controls, 96 JSON/TOON reports, max 71 estimated tokens/284 bytes. Namespace-binding remedies also bring the existing parent/arc maximum to 71/284; other prior metrics unchanged. Complete SDK read-back and tracker byte SHA256 unchanged; runtime raster/network calls 0. Reproduction and provenance in docs/semantic-assets-validation.md. No new mutable/import/sync, lease or transaction path introduced."
  "2026-10-29T06:47:06.845Z",codex-agent,"Both linked commands now have passing receipts: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/semantic-assets.test.ts test/package-banners.test.ts (16/16); node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/semantic-review.test.ts test/contrast.test.ts (20/20). Retried only the second via pm test --run --only-index 2 --timeout 300 --progress; it passed after 150 seconds. The earlier default-budget timeout remains documented; no tests, assertion thresholds or numeric-performance limits changed. Automatic result tracking remains disabled by existing policy, so receipts are explicit comments. Changed files and docs linked. No pm SDK defect found. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress. Exact-head full npm/Bun release CI URL, counts and captured artifact digest will be on PR 27 after final push; existing two-worker coverage limit retained."
